    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1855/graduate-academic-advisor-%28tampa-campus%29/job": {
      "title": "Graduate Academic Advisor (Tampa Campus)",
      "description": "Graduate Academic Advisor (Tampa Campus) ID 2026-1855 Job Locations US-FL-Tampa Category Academic Advising Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Graduate Academic Advisor advises students on academic programs, curriculum, college and university academic policies and procedures. The advisor works directly with graduate students in a variety of disciplines to foster their academic success. The advisor will be the student’s single point of contact on all matters from enrollment to graduation and their success will be measured primarily in terms of retention outcomes. The advisor will assist students individually and in groups via the phone, appointments, or off-site meetings. Essential Responsibilities Provide single point of contact advising service to an assigned group of students from admission through graduation to retain students. In addition, students should be supported to access wraparound supports available as needed and through academic and personal challenge areas. Effectively communicate the curriculum and graduation requirements for program, college and university academic policies and procedures. Provide students with general information on the university that students need to be successful and be an active participant in all campus events and engagement. Build collaborative relationships with academic program faculty, Department Chairs and staff to ensure a cohesive student experience. Participates in department and college meetings as needed. Maintain accurate and timely student records and perform and interpret degree audits including ensuring that student registrations are processed in a timely manner each term. Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree, required Master's Degree, preferred At least one year of experience in academic advising, counseling or other student support role, ideally in a higher education setting Familiarity and experience working with Microsoft Office tools (i.e. Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.) Excellent written and oral communication skills are essential NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $43,631 to $61,084 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) Current NLU employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1861/data-analyst/job": {
      "title": "Data Analyst",
      "description": "Data Analyst ID 2026-1861 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category Analytics/Project Management Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Data Analyst will be responsible for developing and executing on analyses and reporting to drive efficient and effective use of data for a wide variety of data initiatives and requests throughout the university. This position will work in collaboration with team members in the department to execute on the data strategy for the Strategic Data Center and wider university strategic initiatives. This position will engage in various aspects of data collection, cleaning, analysis, metrics, visualizations, documentation, and presentations. The data analyst will work to insure scalability, sustainability, and integrity within NLU data practices and policies. This position will also be involved in knowing and carrying out NLU data governance policy and procedure. Essential Responsibilities Complete data requests and produce various reports and dashboards in a variety of formats (Power BI, Tableau, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, etc.) Conduct strategic analyses by querying, cleaning, manipulating, interpreting, visualizing, and presenting data using statistical techniques. Fulfill various ad hoc data requests. In collaboration with various University stakeholders, map data flows, business processes, and perform gap analysis. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Education, Statistics, Social Work, Public Policy, Business, or related field. Minimum of one year (3 years preferred) of experience manipulating large data sets with analytical software and/or coding languages (R, SQL, SAS, etc.) At least 1 year of experience (3 years preferred) building data reports, dashboards, documentation, and presenting data findings At least 1 year of experience (3 years preferred) gathering and understanding data request specifications and delivering data products Minimum of 1 year of experience (3 years preferred) working with data visualization/analytical software (Power BI, Tableau, SAS, etc.) Analytical Thinking: Breaks down problems and issues into sub-components and then assesses the costs, benefits and risks of various options prior to selecting a particular approach. Technical Skills: Possesses the technical skills and knowledge required to perform essential tasks in an efficient and effective manner. Demonstrates the willingness and ability to train or coach others in the technical arena. Project Coordination and Management: Plans, organizes, and coordinates projects of varying scope to achieve defined goals. Sets clear objectives, develops realistic timelines, allocates resources, and monitors progress. Adapts to changing needs and ensures quality outcomes through effective execution and collaboration. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $53,136 to $77,047 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) NLU Employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1860/assistant-associate-professor-of-special-education-%28graduate-level%29/job": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education (Graduate Level)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education (Graduate Level) ID 2026-1860 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category National College of Education Position Type Faculty Overview THE OPPORTUNITY The National College of Education (NCE) at National Louis University (NLU) seeks a knowledgeable, experienced, and dynamic educator for a full-time 10-Month Special Education faculty position at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank. NLU’s recently updated graduate program offers multiple pathways to earn a master’s degree and/or licensure in special education, including MEd and MAT programs. This position includes teaching current and prospective special educators and preparing candidates to develop strong foundations in culturally sustaining classroom instruction and assessment to meet their students' needs. The successful candidate will engage in disability-affirming teaching and curriculum development and engage in service to the program and college. The candidate must be comfortable with and effective at working with students from different backgrounds, have a strong understanding of special education laws and regulations, have demonstrated classroom experience, and have knowledge of current trends in special education, such as high-leverage teaching practices. The ideal candidate will cultivate a research agenda that furthers social and educational justice for students with disabilities. WHO WE ARE NLU’s National College of Education (NCE) understands that serving PreK-12 students as teachers and school leaders is a calling, a commitment, and a career. Our unique style of partnership with students at all levels—from new teacher preparation to advanced professional programs to doctoral degrees—guides all we do as we create today’s teachers and tomorrow’s leaders. Our programs are designed with the needs of our students in mind. Graduates frequently cite the National College of Education’s top quality professors, convenient locations, flexible course offerings and affordability. Most of all, the commitment to “real world” progressive education is unparalleled. NCE graduates make a difference. Our educators are found in 40% of Illinois public schools and 75% of Chicago Public Schools, collectively impacting the lives of 60,000 students each year. At NCE, our commitment to learning includes ourselves. We have recently created four new programs and evolved an additional 21 programs to more appropriately address the needs of today’s educators. WHO YOU ARE You are: A Change Leader. You are an accomplished PreK-12 educator with a passion for developing students and teachers to their fullest potential. You are an experienced leader who has successfully guided schools and/or district through change. You are a constructive partner who leads the work that needs to be done and advocates for high quality education. You are a veteran educator attracted to university teaching as a new career step and a new level of positive influence on American education. You are deeply motivated by a desire to work in a learning community that is preparing the next generation of life-changing leaders. You will: Model and Support Research. You believe in the power of practitioner researchers. You will draw upon current research to inform your instruction. You will use your research agenda to model research methodologies for our candidates. You will support our candidates as they become research practitioners. You are ready to: Make an Impact. Each and every day, this program changes lives. You want to be a part of NCE’s societally impactful leadership as an educator preparation institution. You are someone who will always look for creative ways for students to earn success. We know this work is challenging, but we are in it together and you are inspired by the opportunity to work collaboratively with other educational leaders to optimize our impact together. Essential Responsibilities Maintaining a teaching load of 24 semester hours of graduate courses across Fall, Winter, and Spring terms. Teaching includes developing and teaching core special education and related courses, and creating and fostering an inclusive learning environment for all students, as well as advising and mentoring graduate students on their academic and professional goals. Contributing to the university through service, including mentoring and advising responsibilities for graduate students, service to the department through program improvement and development, program recruitment, and program accreditation efforts, service to the college (e.g., through committee work), and service to the larger university, community, and profession. Supporting and leading efforts at the course, department, college, and university levels to address educational justice using an intersectional lens. Efforts include curriculum improvement and development as well as departmental and university committees, initiatives, and activities related to advancing excellence in accessible education for all students. Maintaining and enhancing community engagement and existing partnerships with community agencies and schools. This includes working alongside other faculty members, leadership, and students to build relationships with administrators, teachers, and community organization leaders. Engaging in the thought leadership responsibilities of a professional practice faculty member. This includes but is not limited to collaborating with colleagues on curriculum and course development, grant proposals, and extracurricular activities as well as maintaining expertise in the areas of special education research, policy, and practice. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Special Education or related Education or Learning fields. Subject to administrative approval, applicants who are ABD may be considered provided they can demonstrate documented progress toward completion and the ability to successfully defend their dissertation by August 2027 A minimum of 5 years of PreK-22 teaching experience across various special education settings. Demonstrated experience in and/or commitment to advancing equity initiatives within an educational setting and the integration of pedagogies/alignment with the Illinois Culturally Responsive Teaching and Leading (CRTL) standards. Preferred Experiential Qualifications: Experience with assistive and instructional technology. Experience teaching across modalities, including online, virtual/hybrid, and in-person/on-campus. Expertise in teaching literacy, math, and practicum courses required in our programs. Experience working with students with high and low-incidence disability designations at the PreK-22 level. Expertise in Practice-Based Teaching (PBT) and High-Leverage and Evidence-based Practices (HLPs). Experience with collaborative, participatory, community, or action research methodologies and practices. Recent graduates are encouraged to apply. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time faculty benefits can be found here . NLU Faculty salaries are based on rank within each college. The ranges for each rank for the National College of Education are listed below: 2026 NCE 10-Month Faculty Salary Ranges Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, current/previous faculty rank, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please include the following with your application: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts (Official or Unofficial) Optional Additional Attachments: Teaching Philosophy Sample Syllabus Additional Licenses/Certifications Course Evaluations Letters of Recommendation Please note: Upon hire, official transcripts are required and must be sent from the institution(s) directly to the HR Department Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1859/outreach-%26-enrollment-specialist%2c-tampa-campus/job": {
      "title": "Outreach & Enrollment Specialist, Tampa Campus",
      "description": "Outreach & Enrollment Specialist, Tampa Campus ID 2026-1859 Job Locations US-FL-Tampa Category Admissions/Enrollment Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: This position will be responsible for executing the Enrollment and Outreach strategic plan to meet and exceed new student enrollment goals. As such, primary job functions for this position include: 1) building relationships with school and outside organization partners 2) participating and conducting local and regional recruitment events and 3) working with students to ensure they successfully move through the enrollment process. Essential Responsibilities Maintains a high level of knowledge regarding program and the enrollment process and is able to communicate, both orally and in written form, NLU’s admission requirements, program offerings, basic financial aid requirements, and scholarship opportunities with any prospective students as well as stakeholders. Contacts prospective students and determines their educational need. Assess and promptly responds to the needs and concerns of prospective students, via email, social media, phone and in person. Monitor systems tasks list to ensure all inquiries and tasks are completed in a timely manner. Meet or exceed high contact strategy plan. Prepares reports of activities and tracking of prospects' and suspects' inquiries, applications, and student outcomes up to and including enrollment. Builds relationships and act as the primary point of contact for partners to build knowledge of NLU community and generate inquiries. Actively pursues new educational partners for NLU through outreach and networking activities. Develops and maintains a network of relationships that will serve to increase enrollment, such as alumni, current students, the business community, professional organizations, and student groups. Actively plans, attends and documents attendance at information sessions, school and district events, education fairs and community events. Provides feedback and recommendations to management regarding recruiting strategies, customer service, communication, and recruitment programs. Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. 1-3 years of experience working with students in an educational setting and/or experience in a sales environment. 1-3 year of experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Additionally experienced Student Information Systems. Knowledge of social media tools such as Instagram, Snapchat, Facebook and Twitter. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $48,431 to $67,803 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) NLU Employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1858/student-finance-representative-%28tampa-campus%29/job": {
      "title": "Student Finance Representative (Tampa Campus)",
      "description": "Student Finance Representative (Tampa Campus) ID 2026-1858 Job Locations US-FL-Tampa Category Student Finance Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: National Louis University is seeking applicants interested in joining our team as a Student Finance Representative . This position is responsible for reviewing student files, evaluating financial aid applications, awarding and advising students on their eligibility for Title IV funding. Positions assigned to this classification will have a high technical knowledge of financial aid programs and procedures to independently assist students and peers over the phone and via electronic correspondence. The position requires analytical skills and the ability to work independently and with a sense of urgency. In addition, the position requires that all job responsibilities are completed accurately and compliantly in accordance with Title IV regulations. Essential Responsibilities Comply with all Federal, State, and institutional policies and procedures. Ability to understand and interpret Title IV regulations. Ensure NLU’s continued compliance as established by accrediting agencies, state entities and current established company targets. Review all student financial aid files for completeness, accuracy and ensure verification requirements are met. Perform outreach to students as need in order to advise them on their financial aid eligibility and potential funding options. Post related award data into student information system to ensure timely and accurate disbursements. Calculate award grant and loan eligibility using a borrower based academic year (BBAY) or standard academic year (SAY) and certify federal and private student loans. Maintain knowledge of Federal Student Aid and internal University awarding, disbursing, and refund regulations. Perform verification of student financial aid eligibility as needed Maintain and coordinates awarding and student aging reports and actively outreach student to resolve issue. Accurately advise students on BBAY and SAY loan eligibility. Review, analyze, and provide solutions to escalated student issues and communicate proposed solutions back to the appropriate party. Identify areas of opportunities to management and work on developing potential solutions. Ensure ethical and accurate documentation and record keeping which meets all company and regulatory agency standards. Provide exceptional customer service to both internal and external customers via phone and email. Participate as an active team member of the Student Finance Office and ensure active communication and cohesive working relationships with all other departments. Qualifications High School Diploma/GED plus significant related work experience required. Associates or Bachelor's degree preferred. Minimum of 1 year of related experience Customer Focus - Personally demonstrates that external (or internal) customers are a high priority. Identifies customer needs and expectations and responds to them in a timely and effective manner. Anticipates and prevents delays or other things that can adversely affect the customer. Keeps customers informed about the status of pending actions and inquires about customer satisfaction with products or services. Flexibility - Adjusts quickly and effectively to changing conditions and demands. Discusses change as a necessary and inevitable aspect of organizational life as well as an opportunity to learn new things. Has a similar view and approach to potentially stressful situations. Invests personal energy toward accepting and adapting to change that others use toward resisting or resenting it. Problem Solving - Takes a proactive approach to anticipating and preventing problems. When problems occur, defines those problems, investigates obstacles, gathers relevant information, decides whether solving the problem should be a group decision, generates and analyzes alternate solutions and arrives at a workable solution. Quality of Work - Has established a track record of producing work that is highly accurate, demonstrates attention to detail and reflects well on the organization. Is personally committed to high quality work and encourages others to have similar standards. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $20.16 to $28.22 per hour (typical workweek is 37.5 hours). Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) NLU Employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1857/student-engagement-systems-coordinator/job": {
      "title": "Student Engagement Systems Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Engagement Systems Coordinator ID 2026-1857 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category Student Services/Engagement Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Student Engagement Systems Coordinator serves as the primary administrator for the University's student engagement platform and supports student involvement initiatives through technology, training, reporting, and operational support. The position manages student organization records, event processes, system configuration, user access, communications, and engagement reporting while providing training and consultation to students, faculty, and staff. This role partners with Student Affairs stakeholders to enhance student engagement, improve operational effectiveness, and support institutional goals related to student involvement and co-curricular learning. Essential Responsibilities Student Engagement Platform Administration: Serve as the primary administrator for the university's student engagement platform (involve U – Campus groups). Manage user accounts, permissions, organization records, forms, and system configurations. Support student organizations and campus departments in utilizing platform features and services. Coordinate organization registration, event management, attendance tracking, and related operational processes. Troubleshoot issues and serve as liaison with the platform vendor on system enhancements and resolution of technical concerns. Training, Consultation & Support: Develop and deliver training for students, faculty, and staff on effective use of the student engagement platform. Create and maintain user guides, documentation, and educational resources. Provide consultation regarding student organization management, event processes, and platform best practices. Promote adoption and effective utilization of engagement technology across the institution. Reporting & Assessment: Generate and distribute reports related to student engagement, event participation, organization activity, and co-curricular involvement. Monitor data quality and maintain accurate system records. Assist with assessment efforts by gathering and analyzing engagement data. Support departmental and institutional reporting needs related to student involvement and engagement outcomes. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Higher Education Administration, Information Systems, Educational Technology, Business Administration, Communications, Student Affairs or other related field, required Minimum of one year of experience administering software platforms databases, or student information systems in higher education or a comparable environment At least one year of experience providing technical support, troubleshooting and customer service to diverse users One year of experience designing and facilitating trainings, workshops or user education programs Experience collecting analyzing and reporting data to support assessment and decision making Experience managing projects, workflows, or operational processes requiring strong attention to detail and organization Ability to provide responsive, professional, and solution-focused support to diverse users including the ability to effectively diagnose issues, communicates technical information clearly, and promote a positive user experience This position is based at the Chicago campus and may require occasional travel to other NLU locations. Some evening and weekend hours may be required to support student programs, trainings, campus events, and student organization activities. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $43,631 to $61,084 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) Current NLU employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1862/student-success-coach/job": {
      "title": "Student Success Coach",
      "description": "Student Success Coach ID 2026-1862 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category Undergraduate College Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Student Success Coach is an integral component of the signature undergraduate student experience at NLU, actively working towards supporting student transitions, persistence toward graduation, student's satisfaction and sense of belonging and sustainable employment in their major upon completion. The Coach will be responsible for providing intensive academic advising and support to a caseload of approximately 125 undergraduate students and serving as a guide for academic, career, and personal success, while also connecting the students to wraparound supports and university resources. The ideal coach will be proactive in communicating with students and building confidence around their ability to persist at the post-secondary level and successfully transition to the workforce post bachelor’s degree. The role includes proactive direct student advising, ensuring students stay on-track and meet academic milestone and degree requirements. The Coach works in close partnership with faculty and several other University departments to provide students a comprehensive support model and effective referrals. Additionally, the Coach provides and promotes opportunities for community-building and learning through out-of-classroom student programming. The Coach must be an influential, passionate, equity-minded individual with experience working with first-generation and underrepresented college students to drive change and problem-solve. The candidate must have a general belief that all students have the ability to succeed and be personally driven to change the opportunity gap that currently exists in education and presents barriers toward a successful transition to college and persistence towards graduation. Essential Responsibilities Provide direct academic advising and coaching support to a caseload of undergraduate students from their transition to NLU until graduation. Coaches should ensure students are meeting their degree requirements by registering them for courses, modifying their degree plans on a quarterly basis, and effectively communicating the curriculum and graduation requirements for each major and in accordance with university policies. As well as provide additional guidance on maintaining satisfactory academic standing for students entering academic warning, suspension or probation. Coaches should support students in major selection and career exploration as well as help build a student’s self advocacy on campus by helping them access wraparound supports available as needed and be actively engaged in referral process, and follow-up. Coaches should use in-person engagement (sometimes modified to virtual face-to-face engagement) and technology (texting and calls) for interventions to stay in close communication with their caseload of students – using developmental and intrusive advising practices as well as motivational interviewing when students are struggling to overcome barriers. As well as maintaining accurate and timely student records in platforms such as: BANNER, EAB, and Smartsheets, for which training will be provided. Build collaborative relationships with departments chairs, faculty and Career Bridge staff to ensure a cohesive student experience for caseload. Attend Student Success Collaboration meetings and Career Success Team meetings regularly in order to provide a bridge between students, faculty, and career development. Share planning and execution responsibilities for the following coaching team led events: Summer Melt, Y1 Majors Exploration Day, Flight Night, Y2-Y3 Registration and Transition events, Study Tables, Ramp Week, Summer and Winter Melt programming. Assists in participation in and/or promotion of events, programming and services offered by other University departments such as Student Engagement, Career Bridge, Learning Support, Office of Disability and Access Services, Student Finance Office and more. Works with the Director of Student Success and Manager of Student Success to maintain and revise the student support model and wraparound resources to best serve students’ needs while being open to changing policies and practices as needed. Other duties as assigned to support student transitions, persistence toward graduation, student's satisfaction and sense of belonging and sustainable employment in their major upon completion. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Education Counseling, Social work, or closely related field. Master's Degree preferred Two-Four (2-4) years professional experience in advising, teaching, counseling, social work or related field. One-three (1-3) years teaching or staff experience at the high school or college level. One-three (1-3) years experience working with diverse student population. Work Environment/Physical Demands/Travel Requirement: Collaborative office environment with varied duties requiring multi-tasking and dealing with ambiguity at times. Candidate should be equally comfortable spending time working independently, speaking in front of large groups of students, and collaborating with a team at frequent meeting and strategy sessions. This position may require travel between the Chicago and Wheeling campuses. Candidate should be willing to communicate via text/phone with students at night and on weekends NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $48,431,00 to $67,803.00 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) Current NLU employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1856/marketing-manager%2c-online-presence-and-brand-management/job": {
      "title": "Marketing Manager, Online Presence and Brand Management",
      "description": "Marketing Manager, Online Presence and Brand Management ID 2026-1856 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category Marketing/Communications Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Marketing Manager develops, implements, and evaluates integrated marketing and communications initiatives that support the mission, programs, and strategic priorities of the McCormick Institute for Early Childhood (MIEC). Serving as the Institute's primary marketing resource, the position is responsible for marketing planning, digital communications, website management, brand stewardship, audience engagement, and performance measurement. Working collaboratively with Institute leadership and university partners, the Marketing Manager designs and executes multi-channel marketing strategies that increase awareness, strengthen engagement, promote programs and services, and support organizational goals. The role combines strategic planning with hands-on execution, ensuring that marketing activities are aligned with audience needs, institutional priorities, and brand standards. Essential Responsibilities Marketing Planning & Campaign Management Develop and implement integrated marketing plans that align with MIEC's mission, goals, and strategic priorities. Plan, coordinate, and execute multi-channel marketing campaigns utilizing digital, email, social media, web, print, and other communication channels. Collaborate with Institute leadership to identify marketing opportunities, audience needs, and communication priorities. Develop annual marketing objectives, campaign plans, and performance measures to support program and organizational goals. Manage project timelines and coordinate marketing activities to ensure timely and effective execution. Evaluate campaign performance and recommend improvements to strengthen future marketing initiatives. Digital Presence & Website Management Manage and maintain MIEC's website and related digital platforms to ensure content accuracy, usability, accessibility, and alignment with organizational objectives. Coordinate website updates, content enhancements, and improvements to support audience engagement and user experience. Develop and publish website content that promotes MIEC programs, services, resources, events, and initiatives. Apply best practices related to digital communications, search visibility, and audience engagement. Monitor website performance and recommend enhancements based on user behavior and analytics. Brand Management & Communications Develop marketing and communication materials that support the Institute's mission and reflect university brand standards. Ensure consistency of messaging, visual identity, and communication practices across marketing channels. Create and coordinate content for newsletters, publications, promotional materials, and other communication vehicles. Support efforts to strengthen awareness and understanding of MIEC's programs, services, and impact among internal and external audiences. Serve as a resource to Institute staff regarding marketing, communications, and brand-related best practices. CRM, Audience Engagement & Marketing Analytics Partner with Institute and university stakeholders to support CRM-enabled marketing, audience outreach, and engagement initiatives. Develop audience segmentation strategies and communication plans that support recruitment, participation, and relationship-building goals. Monitor and analyze marketing performance data across campaigns and communication channels. Prepare reports, dashboards, and summaries that provide insights into marketing effectiveness and audience engagement. Use analytics and stakeholder feedback to identify opportunities for improvement and inform future planning efforts. Student Staff Supervision & Collaboration Recruit, train, assign, and oversee student workers supporting marketing and communication activities. Provide coaching, direction, and feedback to ensure quality work and professional development. Coordinate projects with internal stakeholders, university partners, vendors, consultants, and external service providers. Foster collaborative relationships that support successful execution of marketing and communication initiatives Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Marketing, Communications, Public Relations, Digital Media, Journalism, Business, or a related field 5+ plus years of progressively responsible professional experience in marketing, communications, digital marketing, brand management, or related areas. Experience developing and executing integrated marketing campaigns. Experience managing websites, digital communications, and social media platforms. Experience analyzing marketing data and utilizing performance metrics to inform decision-making. Experience creating print and digital marketing materials. Experience coordinating multiple projects with competing deadlines. Experience in higher education, nonprofit, or mission-driven organizations, preferred. Experience using CRM and marketing automation platforms, preferred. Experience managing external vendors, agencies, or freelance resources, preferred. Experience supervising student employees, interns, or project-based staff, preferred. Knowledge of accessibility, web content management systems, and digital engagement strategies, preferred. Bilingual in English and Spanish preferred Work Environment/Physical Demands/Travel Requirements: This is hybrid position located at any one of the NLU campuses (Chicago, Lisle or Wheeling). Long periods of sitting, standing, and constant computer/data entry work and the ability to travel 2-3 times per year to represent MIEC as an exhibitor at local, state, or national conferences is a part of the role. Ability to lift 25-30 lbs. is a required element of this position, as well as the ability to stand for long periods while organizing, collating, and stocking/restocking marketing collateral. This position requires some availability during evenings and weekends and reliable access to the Internet and phone when out of the office/working remotely. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $53,136 to $77,047 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Optional) Current NLU employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nl.icims.com/jobs/1864/development-associate%2c-annual-fund/job": {
      "title": "Development Associate, Annual Fund",
      "description": "Development Associate, Annual Fund ID 2026-1864 Job Locations US-IL-Chicago Category Alumni Relations/Fundraising and Development Position Type Staff (Full-Time) Overview Who We Are: For 140 years, National Louis University has been driven by one core belief: education changes lives. Since our founding, we've stayed grounded in the values of innovation, access, excellence, and equity, and we've never wavered from the idea that education is the greatest lever for social and economic mobility. We are a student-focused community built on continuous improvement and a genuine commitment to serving those we teach. Through education, we empower change and build stronger, healthier communities. Our hard-working team runs on collaboration and mutual respect, for one another and for every student we serve. What You Will Do: The Development Associate, Annual Fund supports the goals of the Advancement/Development Department at National Louis University by advancing annual fundraising efforts that increase philanthropic support from alumni, donors, faculty, staff, students, and friends of the University. Reporting to the Director of Annual Giving, this position helps execute annual giving strategies that grow donor participation, retention, and revenue through campaign implementation, donor stewardship, prospect research, reporting and analysis, and project coordination. Working collaboratively across the Advancement team, the Development Associate helps build a sustainable pipeline of engaged donors while supporting the University's Annual Giving fundraising priorities. Essential Responsibilities Annual Giving Campaign Management and Donor Engagement: Support the planning, implementation, and evaluation of annual giving initiatives designed to increase philanthropic support. Coordinate annual fund campaigns and donor engagement activities, including giving days, commencement giving, faculty and staff giving, crowdfunding initiatives, donor recognition programs, and student philanthropy efforts. Provide support to the Director of Annual Giving through secondary moves management for donors and prospects. Manage campaign logistics, donor segmentation, stewardship activities, and coordination with internal and external partners to ensure meaningful outreach and successful execution. Reporting, Analysis and Prospect Research: Monitor and evaluate annual giving performance through reporting, data analysis, and donor research. Prepare reports that measure campaign effectiveness, donor participation, retention, and fundraising results. Conduct prospect research and develop donor profiles to support cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies while partnering with Advancement Operations to maintain accurate donor data and reporting. Project, Event and Administrative Coordination: Provide project management and administrative support for annual giving initiatives, including developing project timelines, coordinating vendors, maintaining calendars and shared documentation, supporting donor cultivation and recognition events, managing registrations and logistics, and assisting with other operational activities that contribute to successful fundraising efforts. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Communications, Nonprofit Management, or other related field, required Minimum of 1 year of experience (3 preferred) in alumni relations, annual fund giving, direct mail appeals, communications, customer service, or other related field. Exceptional oral and written communication skills High level of professionalism, integrity, and good judgement High level of proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel Prior knowledge and familiarity with fundraising databases and email marketing (i.e. Salesforce) Teamwork Oriented : Demonstrates strong teamwork and collaboration by contributing ideas and skills, communicating openly, meeting commitments with accuracy and timeliness, and fostering a positive, cooperative environment that supports shared goals and collective success. Managing Multiple Priorities : Effectively balances competing tasks, deadlines, and responsibilities. Prioritizes work based on urgency, impact, and alignment with goals. Adjusts focus as needed while maintaining quality, communication, and follow-through. Results Oriented : Focuses on achieving meaningful outcomes through disciplined execution, prioritization, and follow-through. Aligns actions with goals, monitors progress, and adapts as needed to deliver high-quality results. NLU Inclusion Statement: National Louis University is deeply committed to serving its community, advancing access and equity, and ensuring that all individuals are welcomed and valued. We are dedicated to fostering a culture where diversity, equity, and inclusion remain at the core of who we are. These are more than just words to us: they are truly a way of life for the NLU community. We recognize that differences in abilities, age, ethnicity, gender (identity and expression), race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, and background bring richness to our work environment. We affirm diverse perspectives, innovative contributions, and authentic presentations of self from every member within the NLU community. We believe inclusion is grounded in the actions we intentionally take each day. Our goal is to inspire and empower NLU employees and community members to cultivate an environment where we collectively focus on uplifting and advancing our institutional culture. Compensation and Benefits At National Louis University, we offer our employees an innovative environment to work together and inspire the ideas that will make an impact. As our external environment changes, our employees are provided the opportunities and tools needed to grow both personally and professionally to remain successful. NLU employees and dependents are offered a wide range of benefits, including but not limited to, Health Insurance benefits, Retirement benefits, Paid Time Off and Educational Opportunities. Additional information regarding full-time staff benefits can be found here . The salary range of the grade for this position is $48,431 to $67,803 annually. Compensation decisions are dependent upon the facts and circumstances of each position and candidate. Offers are based on multiple factors permitted by law, including but not limited to: budgetary considerations, job-related knowledge/skills, experience, market considerations, tenure and standing with the university (applicable to current employees), and internal equity. Application Instructions Please Include the following along with your application: Resume (Required) Cover Letter (Required) Current NLU employees please also submit an Internal Posting Form Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
